# p_a4f7 — Tablet at the Counter During Work Hours, Not the Coffee Table (fork of p_5d8b)

This fork of p_5d8b corrects the tablet's resting place during weekday work hours. The parent's prediction of coffee_table_l1 has now accumulated 2 additional "against" sightings since the last call (bringing the total to 7 against, 1 for across the full log). Meanwhile, the per-object statistics show the tablet's most common location is counter_k1 (5 of 11 sighted days), and during weekday 9–17h the robot found the tablet at counter_k1 on 3 of 9 looks. The kitchen-table hypothesis (p_9c2e) has also failed (0 for, 6 against), and the "tablet travels" hypothesis (p_3a7f) is contradicted by 3 in-house sightings during 9–14.

What changed from p_5d8b: (1) tablet_mara's default location is now counter_k1 instead of coffee_table_l1. (2) The evening couch block (19–22h) is retained. (3) The tablet claim now expects counter_k1 during weekday 9–14. The interpretation: Mara leaves the tablet on the kitchen counter during the day (perhaps as a reference for recipes, messages, or a second screen after work), and only picks it up to the couch in the evening for entertainment.

What sets this apart from p_5d8b: at 11:00 on a weekday, the tablet is at counter_k1 (not coffee_table_l1). What would refute it: the tablet found at the coffee table during weekday 9–14, or found at the kitchen table during that window.

